  "rationale": "Block h1_0:traverse, h2_1:reach and h2_0:obtain (h1_2:traverse also works for the last one). Blocking h1_0 stops h2_2, h3_0 and h3_2, which kills the h4_2 path, and with h2_2 gone, blocking h2_1 stops h4_0. Blocking h2_0 then stops h4_1, so every parent of crown:obtain is cut. Two blocks are not enough. Cutting h4_0 alone takes either h4_0 itself or two blocks (h2_1 plus h2_2 or h1_0). If two blocks go to h2_1 and h1_0 or h2_2, h4_1 still opens through h2_0. If one block is h4_0, a single extra block cannot cut both h4_1 (it needs h4_1 itself, or h2_2/h1_0 plus h2_0/h1_2) and h4_2 at once."
